      "content": "It is definitely an aggressive process, and while excess LDL is the primary culprit, it's not the only thing that can cause arterial buildup. High blood pressure, smoking, and diabetes are all major contributors, acting like other irritants that make the artery walls more vulnerable to those LDL particles. These other factors can make the walls more prone to damage, allowing the cholesterol to latch on more easily, which is why managing overall heart health is key.",
